<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY — a comment ABOVE the root
        breaks `sf` deploy at conversion with a misleading "unable to find matching parent
        xml file" error.

        ADDED 2026-08-30, BA Gap-Closure code-review pass (GATE A durable-audit follow-up,
        user-approved). GATE A (see Broker_Protection_Config__mdt.Protection_Window_Days__c's
        own header) made PropertyMatchingService log the RESOLVED protection window at WARN on
        every claim run, so a disputed claim could be reconstructed from logs after the fact.
        In practice that needs an active trace flag on an ASYNC context user at exactly the
        right moment, which will typically not exist — a debug log is not a durable audit
        trail. This field makes the audit durable by writing the value onto the record itself,
        once, at the moment it mattered.

        Matches Broker_Protection_Config__mdt.Protection_Window_Days__c's type exactly
        (Number(3,0)) so the stamped value and the CMDT source can never disagree on shape.

        🔴 A concurrent developer-agent workstream stamps this field from PropertyClaimService
        at claim time under this EXACT API name — do not rename it.

        🔴 CORRECTED 2026-08-30 (BA Gap-Closure follow-up) - THREE WRITE PATHS, NOT ONE. The
        description below originally said "copied once... and never updated afterward", which
        was accurate only against PropertyClaimService.registerWinner (the new-winner insert),
        the sole path that existed when this field was written. PropertyClaimService.adopt()
        also calls the same stampResolvedWindow helper, on BOTH of its callers - the orphan-
        adoption leg and the expired-adoption leg (registerWinner's catch block and claim()'s
        expired-registry check). adopt() already resets Registered_DateTime__c on every call,
        because an adoption genuinely IS a fresh claim, not a continuation of the old one; RE-
        stamping Protection_Window_Days__c alongside it is required by the same logic, not an
        inconsistency - leaving the original insert's stamp in place would produce a row whose
        Registered_DateTime__c and whose Protection_Window_Days__c came from two different
        claims. That mismatch would be worst on exactly the expired-adoption leg, which is the
        GATE A dispute scenario (a claim outliving its own window) this field exists to settle.
        So: every write to Registered_DateTime__c is accompanied by a write to this field, on
        all three call sites, each still a single write per property per transaction - this is
        not a periodic or trigger-driven update.
    -->
    <fullName>Protection_Window_Days__c</fullName>
    <description>The broker protection window (in days) that was IN FORCE THE LAST TIME THIS CLAIM WAS REGISTERED - written by automation on every path that sets Registered_DateTime__c (the new-winner insert and both adoption legs; an adoption is a fresh claim), never hand-edited. Copied from Broker_Protection_Config__mdt.Default.Protection_Window_Days__c. Exists so a disputed claim can be settled from this record rather than an expired debug log. The live configured value on the CMDT record may since have changed - that is expected and is the entire point of stamping it here.</description>
    <externalId>false</externalId>
    <inlineHelpText>Protection window in force when this claim was last registered. Written by automation, never hand-edited; the current configured value may differ.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Protection Window Days</label>
    <precision>3</precision>
    <required>false</required>
    <scale>0</scale>
    <type>Number</type>
    <unique>false</unique>
</CustomField>
